<title>JAPAN: Japan 1996 domestic vehicle output up 1.5% yr/yr.</title>
<headline>Japan 1996 domestic vehicle output up 1.5% yr/yr.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-01-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's vehicle production rose 1.5 percent from a year earlier to 10,345,786 units in calendar 1996, the Japan Automobile Manufacturers' Association (JAMA) said on Monday.</p>
<p>It was the first yearly output increase in six years.</p>
<p>The association also said Japan's domestic vehicle production in December rose 9.5 percent from a year earlier to 846,626 vehicles, the fourth straight month in which output rose on a year-on-year basis.  </p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of figures in 1996, with percentage changes:</p>
<p>					 1996	     YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars			     7,863,763	   up    3.3</p>
<p> Trucks			   2,428,897	   down  4.3</p>
<p> Buses				 53,126	   up   12.4</p>
<p>The 1996 production by major manufacturers:</p>
<p>			    1996		YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Toyota Motor	3,410,060	   up    7.5</p>
<p> Nissan Motor	1,610,542	   down  6.0</p>
<p> Mitsubishi Motors 1,200,007	   down  9.6</p>
<p> Honda Motor	 1,092,148	   up   12.9</p>
<p> Mazda Motor	   773,567	   up    0.3</p>
<p> Suzuki Motor	  847,702	   down  1.7</p>
<p> Daihatsu Motor	535,673	   up   12.2</p>
<p> Fuji Heavy	    416,980	   down  0.5</p>
<p> Isuzu Motors	  331,248	   down  4.5</p>
<p> Hino Motors	    78,240	   down  5.5</p>
<p> Nissan Diesel	  49,231	   down 10.9</p>
<p>The following is a breakdown of the figures in December with percentage changes:</p>
<p>					 DEC		YR/YR PCT</p>
<p> Cars				 646,902	   up   10.0</p>
<p> Trucks			     195,625	   up    8.1</p>
<p> Buses				  4,099	   down 11.5</p>
